Recall the difference formula for tangent:

$$
\tan\left(x - y\right) = \frac{\tan x - \tan y}{1 + \tan x\tan y}
$$

Apply it with $x=330^\circ$ and $y=135^\circ$. The special-angle values are $\tan\left(330^\circ\right)=-\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{3}$ and $\tan\left(135^\circ\right)=-1$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
\tan\left(195^\circ\right) &= \tan\left(330^\circ - 135^\circ\right) \\
&= \frac{\tan\left(330^\circ\right) - \tan\left(135^\circ\right)}{1 + \tan\left(330^\circ\right)\tan\left(135^\circ\right)} \\
&= \frac{\left(-\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{3}\right) - \left(-1\right)}{1 + \left(-\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{3}\right)\left(-1\right)}
\end{aligned}
$$

Multiply the numerator and denominator by $3$ to clear the fractions:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\tan\left(195^\circ\right) &= \frac{3\left(\left(-\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{3}\right) - \left(-1\right)\right)}{3\left(1 + \left(-\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{3}\right)\left(-1\right)\right)} \\
&= \frac{3 - \sqrt{3}}{3 + \sqrt{3}}
\end{aligned}
$$

Multiply by the conjugate of the denominator, expand, and simplify:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\tan\left(195^\circ\right) &= \frac{3 - \sqrt{3}}{3 + \sqrt{3}}\cdot \frac{3 - \sqrt{3}}{3 - \sqrt{3}} \\
&= \frac{\left(3 - \sqrt{3}\right)\left(3 - \sqrt{3}\right)}{\left(3 + \sqrt{3}\right)\left(3 - \sqrt{3}\right)} \\
&= \frac{12 - 6\sqrt{3}}{6} \\
&= 2 - \sqrt{3}
\end{aligned}
$$

Recall the sum formula for tangent:

$$
\tan\left(x + y\right) = \frac{\tan x + \tan y}{1 - \tan x\tan y}
$$

Apply it with $x=135^\circ$ and $y=30^\circ$. The special-angle values are $\tan\left(135^\circ\right)=-1$ and $\tan\left(30^\circ\right)=\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{3}$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
\tan\left(165^\circ\right) &= \tan\left(135^\circ + 30^\circ\right) \\
&= \frac{\tan\left(135^\circ\right) + \tan\left(30^\circ\right)}{1 - \tan\left(135^\circ\right)\tan\left(30^\circ\right)} \\
&= \frac{\left(-1\right) + \left(\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{3}\right)}{1 - \left(-1\right)\left(\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{3}\right)}
\end{aligned}
$$

Multiply the numerator and denominator by $3$ to clear the fractions:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\tan\left(165^\circ\right) &= \frac{3\left(\left(-1\right) + \left(\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{3}\right)\right)}{3\left(1 - \left(-1\right)\left(\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{3}\right)\right)} \\
&= \frac{-3 + \sqrt{3}}{3 + \sqrt{3}}
\end{aligned}
$$

Multiply by the conjugate of the denominator, expand, and simplify:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\tan\left(165^\circ\right) &= \frac{-3 + \sqrt{3}}{3 + \sqrt{3}}\cdot \frac{3 - \sqrt{3}}{3 - \sqrt{3}} \\
&= \frac{\left(-3 + \sqrt{3}\right)\left(3 - \sqrt{3}\right)}{\left(3 + \sqrt{3}\right)\left(3 - \sqrt{3}\right)} \\
&= \frac{-12 + 6\sqrt{3}}{6} \\
&= -2 + \sqrt{3}
\end{aligned}
$$

Recall the difference formula for tangent:

$$
\tan\left(x - y\right) = \frac{\tan x - \tan y}{1 + \tan x\tan y}
$$

Apply it with $x=\frac{5\pi}{4}$ and $y=\frac{2\pi}{3}$. The special-angle values are $\tan\left(\frac{5\pi}{4}\right)=1$ and $\tan\left(\frac{2\pi}{3}\right)=-\sqrt{3}$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
\tan\left(\frac{7\pi}{12}\right) &= \tan\left(\frac{5\pi}{4} - \frac{2\pi}{3}\right) \\
&= \frac{\tan\left(\frac{5\pi}{4}\right) - \tan\left(\frac{2\pi}{3}\right)}{1 + \tan\left(\frac{5\pi}{4}\right)\tan\left(\frac{2\pi}{3}\right)} \\
&= \frac{\left(1\right) - \left(-\sqrt{3}\right)}{1 + \left(1\right)\left(-\sqrt{3}\right)}
\end{aligned}
$$

Combining the terms gives

$$
\begin{aligned}
\tan\left(\frac{7\pi}{12}\right) &= \frac{1 + \sqrt{3}}{1 - \sqrt{3}}
\end{aligned}
$$

Multiply by the conjugate of the denominator, expand, and simplify:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\tan\left(\frac{7\pi}{12}\right) &= \frac{1 + \sqrt{3}}{1 - \sqrt{3}}\cdot \frac{1 + \sqrt{3}}{1 + \sqrt{3}} \\
&= \frac{\left(1 + \sqrt{3}\right)\left(1 + \sqrt{3}\right)}{\left(1 - \sqrt{3}\right)\left(1 + \sqrt{3}\right)} \\
&= \frac{4 + 2\sqrt{3}}{-2} \\
&= -2 - \sqrt{3}
\end{aligned}
$$

